# Semgrep uses this file INSTEAD OF its built-in default ignore list once
# any .semgrepignore is present, so the standard defaults are reproduced
# below to avoid widening the scan to vendor/build trees. See
# https://semgrep.dev/docs/ignoring-files-folders-code/ for the upstream
# defaults this mirrors.
.git/
node_modules/
vendor/
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
.nuxt/
.venv/
venv/
.tox/
coverage/
*.min.js
*.min.css
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
bun.lock
Pipfile.lock
poetry.lock

# Recon #18878 classified these files' sole semgrep finding
# (generic.secrets.security.detected-jwt-token) as LIKELY-NOISE: every
# match is a Mapbox `pk.eyJ...` public token or a Supabase anon key, both
# designed for client-side exposure (Mapbox scopes by URL/referrer;
# Supabase anon keys are gated by RLS, not secrecy). Excluded by path
# rather than inline nosemgrep so the lines containing the long-lived
# public tokens are not touched -- editing them would make gitleaks'
# diff-based scan treat pre-existing, unchanged tokens as newly added.
# See issue #18883 for the PR this unblocks.
